= Solution
{parent=a}

In the paper's convention $\mathbf J$ is measured in units of $\hbar$, and $g$ is dimensionless. For $m=-J,-J+1,\ldots,J$, the <magnetic moment> and its <Zeeman energy> are
$$
\boxed{\mu_z=-g\mu_Bm,\qquad E_m=-\mu_zB=g\mu_BBm.}
$$
If $\mathbf J$ instead denotes dimensional angular <momentum>, its coefficient must contain $1/\hbar$. This resolves the units of the printed moment formula.

= b
{parent=B1}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

Write $y=g\mu_BB/(k_BT)$. Summing the <Boltzmann factors> gives the one-atom <partition function>
$$
Z_1=\sum_{m=-J}^Je^{-ym}=\frac{\sinh[(J+1/2)y]}{\sinh(y/2)}.
$$
Since $\langle m\rangle=-\partial_y\log Z_1$, the <Brillouin magnetization formula> is
$$
\boxed{\langle\mu_z\rangle=g\mu_B\left[(J+\tfrac12)\coth((J+\tfrac12)y)-\tfrac12\coth(y/2)\right],\qquad M=N\langle\mu_z\rangle.}
$$
Here $M$ is the total <magnetic moment> used by the question; the <magnetization> per unit volume is $M/V$. For independent distinguishable atoms, $Z_N=Z_1^N$, with no indistinguishability factor.

Putting $J=1/2$ yields
$$
\boxed{M=Ng\mu_B[\coth y-\tfrac12\coth(y/2)]=\frac{Ng\mu_B}{2}\tanh(y/2).}
$$
The apparent singularities of the hyperbolic cotangents at $B=0$ cancel; the finite sum makes the zero-field limit explicit.<Statistical Physics by David Tong>[Chapter 1: canonical partition functions and independent two-state systems]{ref}

= c
{parent=B1}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=c}

For $g>0$, $B\to+\infty$ at fixed $T>0$ selects $m=-J$, so all moments align with the field:
$$
\boxed{M\longrightarrow Ng\mu_BJ.}
$$
This is <magnetic saturation>. The <Curie response of an arbitrary independent spin> follows at weak field: $\coth z=z^{-1}+z/3+O(z^3)$ gives
$$
\boxed{M=\frac{N(g\mu_B)^2J(J+1)}{3k_BT}B+O(B^3)\longrightarrow0.}
$$
This is the <Curie law> of independent moments with <paramagnetism>. Thermal populations are symmetric at zero field, so the model has no spontaneous <magnetization>. Both limits hold at fixed positive <temperature>; taking $T\to0$ first is a different limiting procedure.

